C     Command-line processing offset for most Unix-like systems
      INTEGER MORG
      PARAMETER (MORG=0)


C     MORG- offset value for the first command-line argument.
C           On PC systems this should be 1 if the supplied 
C           routines for retrieval of command-line arguments
C           are used.  If the compiler differs from Lahey,
C           then the value should be set to get the first
C           file argument.  On Unix systems MORG=0 is normally
C           required. 

